<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!-- TEST interface, quest tooltips rebuilt one piece at a time (user, 2026-10-19: "lets go step
     by step, one interface at a time, until we can find *SOME* kind of change"). Deployed as
     FCJH_QTest.StormInterface beside FCJH; none of FCJH's files are in it.

     Step 1: a copy of Blizzard's own leader panel (the Tab panel, whose quest tooltips fill),
     untouched: Blizzard's template, placed as Blizzard places its own (gameui.stormlayout:913),
     only 150 lower so it can be told from Blizzard's. Control+Shift+Q sends it Show / Hide,
     as Tab does Blizzard's. Its Talents tab, then hover a quest icon:
       - fills: a copy gets the quest info, so our earlier tries broke it with what they changed
       - blank: a copy doesn't, whatever is done to it
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 7be15cc): "a lower talents table. It has the default quests. It
     has tooltips". A copy gets the quest info.

     Step 2, one change: opened as Ahli's (and all eight tries) were, not Blizzard's way. Its
     box on from load (HeroLeaderPanelContainer Visible), the toggle fading it in and sliding
     it from 4400 below (and Init / InitEnd, as Ahli's), no Show event sent. Blank: the panel
     must be sent Show.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 5d1ae3f): on screen from load by itself, "icons still load.
     tooltips are still attached". No Show needed.

     Step 3, one change: every row's two quest icons lifted out of the panel, re-anchored in a
     line across the top of the screen (blue's five, then red's), the panel left as it is.
     Fills there: an icon keeps its tooltip away from its panel (the user's idea: an
     off-screen copy, its icons lifted onto ours).
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, f2696bb): "i dont see any icons at all, no tooltips seem to react
     anywhere" - as tries 3 and 4, where a lifted icon never drew either.

     Step 3b, one change: the same lift, each icon and every part of it Unclipped. A frame
     draws only inside its parent's box, and the lifted icons sit far outside their row's
     (whose box is turned inside out besides: its right edge follows icon 1 up to the top of
     the screen, left of its own left edge). Shows now: it was clipping. Still nothing:
     an icon can't leave its row.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 9f2e09c): still no icons, and the screenshot shows the "!" column
     empty where steps 1 and 2 had them - the override reaches the icons, they leave the
     column, but don't draw where they land.

     Step 4, one change from step 2: each row's first quest icon (the second follows it, as
     Blizzard's does) kept in its row on Blizzard's own anchors, moved 150 left into the
     blank after the hero's name. The lift and Unclipped of 3 / 3b gone. Shows there: an
     icon can be moved, just not far (something above it clips). Gone again: any re-anchor
     of a quest icon kills it.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 58476c4): "icons came back, but tooltips had a hard time staying
     active" / "they did fill out correctly though". An icon moved within its row draws and
     fills.

     Step 5, one change: the same icons moved 30 up as well, half out of their row into the
     one above. Cut off at the row's edge: the row (or a frame its size) is what clips, so a
     lift has to take the row with it. Drawn whole over the row above: the clip is higher up,
     and the step can be widened.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 048e0f7, screenshot): "icons cut off at the row edge" - the half
     in their own row drawn, the half over the row above not. The row clips.

     Step 6, one change: each row's TalentsContainerFrame Batch false. It is the one frame in
     the row Blizzard batches (Batch true, heroleaderpanel.stormlayout:1717), and a batch
     draws only inside its own box - Spazzo's note blames baseline quests for his batching.
     Whole now: the batch was the clip, and a lift can go far with it off. Still cut: it is
     the row's own box (PlayerFrame), and the row must travel with the icons.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, ad64c31): "still cut off". Not the batch.

     Step 7, one change: each row's TalentsContainerFrame grown 60 above and 60 below the row
     (its middle where it was, so nothing in it moves; SelectionUnitStatusPanel and
     UnitStatusFrame0 are anchored to it and grow with it). Whole now: the clip is that
     chain's box, which we can size as we like - up to the whole screen, for a far lift.
     Still cut: it is the row itself (PlayerFrame).
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 9c04a2f): "still cut off". Not that frame's box.

     Step 8, one change: every frame of the chain under the row Unclipped - TalentsContainer-
     Frame, SelectionUnitStatusPanel, UnitStatusFrame0, HeroSelectedTalentTreeFrame,
     QuestContainerContainerFrame, BaseQuestCenterFrame and the icon (3b freed only the icon
     and its parts, and its ancestors may each clip). Whole now: the chain was clipped link
     by link, and a far lift needs it all Unclipped. Still cut: Unclipped can't get past the
     row - the row must travel.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 270d4a4, screenshot): "that worked" - the icons drawn whole
     across the row line. Clipped link by link; Unclipped all the way down frees them.

     Step 9, one change: step 3's far lift again with the chain freed - each row's first
     quest icon (the second follows it) re-anchored to the screen, a line above the panel
     220 down, blue's five then red's. Shows and fills: icons can go anywhere, and our
     ctrl-1 pane can borrow them. Cut at the panel's edge: the frames above the row
     (PlayerFrame, TabControl, HeroLeaderPanelContainer) clip too.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, c104af4, screenshot): the icons drawn on the line above the
     panel, but "tooltips dont seem to show up anymore". Known (HANDOFF section 3): an icon
     outside its player's box gives no tooltip - drawing and the mouse are checked apart.

     Step 10, one change: FCJH's spread (tools/gen.py, as the talent row's lifted pieces have
     it) on every frame from the row down to the icon - PlayerFrame, TalentsContainerFrame,
     SelectionUnitStatusPanel, UnitStatusFrame0, HeroSelectedTalentTreeFrame,
     QuestContainerContainerFrame, BaseQuestCenterFrame: each stretched over the whole screen,
     mouse and tooltips off, so a lifted icon is inside every box above it. The rows' other
     contents will be thrown about (test only). Fills now: lifted quest icons can keep their
     tooltips anywhere. Still none: the panel above the rows (TabControl,
     HeroLeaderPanelContainer) must be spread too.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 6d04cc2): "no tooltips". As tools/gen.py already has it for the
     talent row's lifted pieces: they give no tooltips however they're shown, and the plates'
     heroic tooltips come from copies whose player box is moved, not the icon (HANDOFF 3).
     Steps 3-10 are a dead end for tooltips.

     Step 11, back to step 2 and one change: the rows moved, not the icons - PlayerFrame0's
     top 200 up (Blizzard's +5 below the sort buttons, now -195); the other nine are chained
     to it and follow. The top rows land above the panel, the rest inside it. Rows above the
     panel draw and fill: rows can be placed onto our ctrl-1 pane. Cut at the panel's top,
     or no tooltips there: the panel's box holds the rows, and the panel itself must move
     (Ahli's way).
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 35d160b, screenshot): the rows moved up but cut at the panel's
     top (Uther and Murky hidden above it, Zarya half cut); Nova's row, moved but still
     inside, "works" - a moved row keeps its quest tooltips.

     Step 12, one change: each row (PlayerFrame0-9) Unclipped, as step 8 freed the icon's
     chain. Rows above the panel drawn, tooltips filling: rows can go anywhere with working
     quests. Still cut: the panel's own frames (TabControl, HeroLeaderPanelContainer) need
     it too.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 787f7f4, screenshot): Uther's and Murky's rows drawn above the
     panel, Murky's quest icon filled ("0"), but "Murky's tooltip is nowhere to be seen,
     Nova's is fine". Drawing outside the panel works; the mouse doesn't - tooltips answer
     only inside the panel's box (HeroLeaderPanelContainer, Blizzard's fixed 1362x823, which
     TabControl fills), as a lifted icon answers only inside its row (steps 9-10).

     Step 13, one idea: grow the box over the rows, not the rows out of it. The container
     400 taller (823 to 1223; it's centred, so its top goes 200 up), and PlayerFrame0 back to
     Blizzard's +5 under the sort buttons, which go up with the box's top - so the rows sit
     about where step 12 put them, now inside the box. Murky's tooltip fills: the box is what
     catches the mouse, and sizing it (art hidden later) puts working rows anywhere.
     Seen (user, 2026-10-19, 8ceaed0): "Both have tooltips" - Murky's and Nova's. The box
     (HeroLeaderPanelContainer's size) is what the mouse answers inside; grown over the
     rows, every row's quest tooltip works.

     Step 14, one change, the first towards our ctrl-1 pane: the panel's background (the
     container's BackgroundImage: mask, glass blur, image) at Alpha 0. Rows over the bare
     screen with tooltips: the art can go and the box stay. Tooltips gone: the background
     (or the container's HitTestFrame behind it) is part of what takes the mouse. -->
<Desc>
	<Frame type="GameUI" name="GameUI" file="GameUI">
		<Frame type="Frame" name="UIContainer">
			<Frame type="Frame" name="ConsoleUIContainer">
				<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanel" name="FCJH_QTestPanel" template="HeroLeaderPanel/HeroLeaderPanelTemplate">
					<Anchor side="Top"    relative="$parent" pos="Min" offset="150"/>
					<Anchor side="Left"   relative="$parent" pos="Min" offset="0"/>
					<Anchor side="Bottom" relative="$parent" pos="Max" offset="150"/>
					<Anchor side="Right"  relative="$parent" pos="Max" offset="0"/>
					<RenderPriority val="520"/>
					<Frame type="Frame" name="HeroLeaderPanelContainer">
						<Visible val="true"/>
						<Height val="1223"/>
						<Frame type="Frame" name="BackgroundImage">
							<Alpha val="0"/>
						</Frame>
						<Frame type="TabControl" name="TabControl">
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame0">
								<Anchor side="Top" relative="$parent/StatsContainerFrame/SortButton0" pos="Max" offset="5"/>
								<Unclipped val="true"/>
							</Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame1"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame2"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame3"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame4"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame5"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame6"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame7"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame8"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
							<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanelPlayerFrame" name="PlayerFrame9"><Unclipped val="true"/></Frame>
						</Frame>
					</Frame>
				</Frame>
				<Frame type="ToggleControl" name="FCJH_QTestToggle">
					<Anchor relative="$parent"/>
					<Shortcut val="Control+Shift+Q"/>
					<AcceptsMouse val="false"/>
					<CollapseLayout val="true"/>
					<Visible val="false"/>
					<Animation name="FCJH_Open">
						<Event event="OnShown" action="DirectionForward,Play"/>
						<Event event="OnHidden" action="DirectionReverse,Play"/>
						<Event event="Init" action="DirectionForward,Play"/>
						<Event event="InitEnd" action="DirectionReverse,Play"/>
						<Controller type="Fade" end="Pause" frame="$parent/FCJH_QTestPanel">
							<Key type="Curve" time="0" value="0"/>
							<Key type="Curve" time="0.1" value="50"/>
							<Key type="Curve" time="0.25" value="255"/>
						</Controller>
						<Controller type="Anchor" end="Pause" frame="$parent/FCJH_QTestPanel" side="Top" relative="true">
							<Key type="Curve" time="0" value="4400" inout="Fast"/>
							<Key type="Curve" time="0.001" value="0" inout="Fast"/>
						</Controller>
						<Controller type="Anchor" end="Pause" frame="$parent/FCJH_QTestPanel" side="Bottom" relative="true">
							<Key type="Curve" time="0" value="4400" inout="Fast"/>
							<Key type="Curve" time="0.001" value="0" inout="Fast"/>
						</Controller>
					</Animation>
				</Frame>
			</Frame>
		</Frame>
	</Frame>
</Desc>
